From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 16:52:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] A desktop mode: -d covers the screen as a
 _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE_DESKTOP window on ~/Desktop

The window fills the screen and is marked as the desktop, so the window
manager keeps it below the other windows, without a frame, on every
virtual desktop.  Directories open in a new window (through the opener)
instead of in place; after 1.5 s without input (and no button held, so
never inside a click, a double click or a drag) the main loop returns
and xfiles re-reads the directory when its ctime has changed, which
shows the files other windows put there.  XFILES_DESKTOP=1 in the
environment tells the control script.
---
